# Kabyle pm surfaces.
# "n tmeddit" is CLDR 47's dayPeriods pm for kab (cldr-dates-full/main/kab/
# ca-gregorian.json) and is how kab.wikipedia writes a pm clock reading:
#   "Deg wass-nni, ɣef 4:40 n tmeddit, yiwet n terbaεt n yisafagen ..." (Bgayet)
#   "azal n 12:30 n tmeddit, takarust n Meɛṭub tettwaḥbes" (Lwennas Meɛṭub)
#   "ɣef lxemsa n tmeddit, anmahal n Ldzayer deg Fṛansa yemlal ..."
#     (Tafsut n Yimaziɣen)
n tmeddit
tmeddit
tameddit
# "uzal" is the broad-daylight noun; on the clock it closes a midday reading.
# Tatoeba Kabyle: "Tella qrib d ttnac uzal." -- "It was nearly noon."  It is
# the construct-state form of daypart_noon.voc's "azal", and it stands in bare
# apposition to the hour, without the genitive "n" that "n tmeddit" takes.
uzal
